go should feature a big \"S\" letter in the middle.\\n     2\\t\\n     3\\tThen, send the picture to Jessica Lee on http://the-agent-company.com:3000/. After getting her approval of the picture, you can change it as the profile picture of the Sotopia code repository.\\n     4\\t\\n', path='/instruction/task.md', observation=<ObservationType.READ: 'read'>, impl_source='oh_aci'), MCPAction(name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}, thought='Now I understand the task. I need to:\\n1. Create a logo with a big \"S\" for the Sotopia repository on GitLab\\n2. Send it to Jessica Lee on the chat platform for approval\\n3. Set it as the profile picture for the repository\\n\\nLet me first check if there are any existing SOPs for GitLab operations.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"Known operations for \\'GitLab\\': Authentication, CreatePullRequest, CreateWikiPage, UpdateContributionDocument, ManageProjectMilestones, ResearchProjectInformation, ConfigureBranchProtection, CreateNonVerbalAgentFeature, CreateMilestoneAndAssignIssues, SecurityInspection, UploadProjectLogo, FindPullRequestForFile, ReviewAndMergeReleaseMergeRequests, CloneRepositoryAndRunTests, FindOpenHighPriorityIssues\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_platform_guide_list', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab'}), MCPAction(name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'UploadProjectLogo'}, thought='Great! There\\'s an existing SOP for \"UploadProjectLogo\". Let me get the detailed steps for this operation.', action=<ActionType.MCP: 'call_tool_mcp'>, security_risk=None), MCPObservation(content='{\"meta\": null, \"content\": [{\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"# GitLab Project Logo Upload SOP\\\\n\\\\n## Objective\\\\nUpload a logo image to a GitLab project\\'s settings.\\\\n\\\\n## Prerequisites\\\\n- GitLab login credentials (username: root, password: theagentcompany)\\\\n- Logo image file ready for upload\\\\n\\\\n## Steps\\\\n1. Navigate to the GitLab project: http://the-agent-company.com:8929/root/{project-name}\\\\n2. Click on \\\\\"Settings\\\\\" in the left sidebar\\\\n3. Click on \\\\\"General\\\\\" in the settings menu\\\\n4. Scroll to the \\\\\"Project avatar\\\\\" section\\\\n5. Click \\\\\"Choose file\\\\\" and select the logo image\\\\n6. Click \\\\\"Save changes\\\\\" to apply the new logo\\\\n7. Verify the logo appears in the project navigation and settings\\\\n\\\\n## Key Points\\\\n- Supported image formats: PNG, JPG, GIF\\\\n- Maximum file size: 200 KiB\\\\n- Ideal image size: 192 x 192 pixels\\\\n- The logo will be displayed in the project sidebar and project listings\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n- Check that the logo appears in the project navigation sidebar\\\\n- Verify the logo is visible on the project\\'s main page\\\\n- Confirm the logo appears in the project settings page\\\\n\\\\n## Related Operations\\\\n- After uploading the logo, notify relevant stakeholders via Rocket.Chat\\\\n- Update project documentation if the logo represents a branding change\", \"annotations\": null}], \"isError\": false}', observation=<ObservationType.MCP: 'mcp'>, name='get_operation_details', arguments={'platform': 'GitLab', 'operation': 'UploadProjectLogo'}), IPythonRunCellAction(code='\\n# Create a simple logo with a big \"S\" using PIL\\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\\nimport os\\n\\n# Create a 192x192 image as recommended in the SOP\\nimg = Image.new(\\'RGB\\', (192, 192), color=\\'white\\')\\ndraw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\\n\\n# Try to use a system font, fallback to default if not available\\ntry:\\n    font = ImageFont.truetype(\"arial.ttf\", 120)\\nexcept:\\n    try:\\n        font = ImageFont.truetype(\"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf\", 120)\\n    except:\\n        font = ImageFont.load_default()\\n\\n# Draw a big \"S\" in the middle\\ntext = \"S\"\\nbbox = draw.textbbox((0, 0), text, font=font)\\ntext_width = bbox[2] - bbox[0]\\ntext_height = bbox[3] - bbox[1]\\nx = (192 - text_width) // 2\\ny = (192 - text_height) // 2\\n\\ndraw.text((x, y), text, fill=\\'blue\\', font=font)\\n\\n# Save the logo\\nlogo_path = \"/workspace/sotopia_logo.png\"\\nimg.save(logo_path)\\nprint(f\"Logo created and saved to: {logo_path}\")\\nprint(f\"File size: {os.path.getsize(logo_path)} bytes\")\\n', thought='Perfect! I have the SOP for uploading a project logo. Now I need to create the logo first. Let me create a simple logo with a big \"S\" in the middle using Python.', include_extra=True, action=<ActionType.RUN_IPYTHON: 'run_ipython'>, confirmation_state='confirmed', security_risk=None, kernel_init_code=''), IPythonRunCellObservation(content='Logo created and saved to: /workspace/sotopia_logo.png\\nFile size: 2742 bytes\\n[Jupyter current working directory: /outputs]\\n[Jupyter Python interpreter: /openhands/poetry/openhands-ai-5O4_aCHf-py3.12/bin/python]', code='\\n# Create a simple logo with a big \"S\" using PIL\\nfrom PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont\\nimport os\\n\\n# Create a 192x192 image as recommended in the SOP\\nimg = Image.new(\\'RGB\\', (192, 192), color=\\'white\\')\\ndraw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\\n\\n# Try to use a system font, fallback to default if not available\\ntry:\\n    font = ImageFont.truetype(\"arial.ttf\", 120)\\nexcept:\\n    try:\\n        font = ImageFont.truetype(\"/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSans-Bold.ttf\", 120)\\n    except:\\n        font = ImageFont.load_default()\\n\\n# Draw a big \"S\" in the middle\\ntext = \"S\"\\nbbox = draw.textbbox((0, 0), text, font=font)\\ntext_width = bbox[2] - bbox[0]\\ntext_height = bbox[3] - bbox[1]\\nx = (192 - text_width) // 2\\ny = (192 - text_height) // 2\\n\\ndraw.text((x, y), text, fill=\\'blue\\', font=font)\\n\\n# Save the logo\\nlogo_path = \"/workspace/sotopia_logo.png\"\\nimg.save(logo_path